# Button System Guidelines

1. All regular action buttons and button links use `.btn`. The shared appearance in `style.css` matches the homepage Search Cars button: solid blue, white 16px semibold text, 12px/24px padding, 8px corners, darker hover/active states and the pale blue focus ring.
2. Existing modifiers (`.btn-primary`, `.btn-primary-gradient`, `.btn-secondary`, `.btn-success`, `.btn-danger`, `.btn-link`, `.btn-lg`) remain valid for markup/JS compatibility and now share the same appearance. Keep action labels and existing confirmation behaviour intact.
3. Component CSS may set width, margins, alignment or wrapping; do not redefine button padding, typography, colour, radius, focus or disabled styling.
4. Keep icon-only utility controls, dropdown fields and navigation links separate from action buttons.
5. Do not introduce new legacy button classes. The homepage filter submit also uses `.btn`, with only its full width controlled locally.
